  "question": {
    "text": "The sum to the infinity of the series $1+\\frac{2}{3}+\\frac{6}{3^2}+\\frac{10}{3^3}+\\frac{14}{3^4}+\\ldots \\ldots$ is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "\n2\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n3\n",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "\n4\n",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\n6",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Let $S=1+\\frac{2}{3}+\\frac{6}{3^2}+\\frac{10}{3^3}+\\frac{14}{3^4}+\\ldots$.\n$\\frac{1}{3} S=\\frac{1}{3}+\\frac{2}{3^2}+\\frac{6}{3^3}+\\frac{10}{3^4}+\\ldots$\nDividing (1) \\& (2)\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n& S\\left(1-\\frac{1}{3}\\right)=1+\\frac{1}{3}+\\frac{4}{3^2}+\\frac{4}{3^3}+\\frac{4}{3^4}+\\ldots . \\\\\n& \\frac{2}{3} S=\\frac{4}{3}+\\frac{4}{3^2}\\left(1+\\frac{1}{3}+\\frac{1}{3^2}+\\ldots . .\\right) \\Rightarrow \\frac{2}{3} S=\\frac{4}{3}+\\frac{4}{3^2}\\left(\\frac{1}{1-\\frac{1}{3}}\\right)=\\frac{4}{3}+\\frac{4}{3^2} \\frac{3}{2}=\\frac{4}{3}+\\frac{2}{3}=\\frac{6}{2} \\Rightarrow \\frac{2}{3} S=\\frac{6}{3} \\Rightarrow S=3\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"
  }
}